    "scientific": "Asimina triloba — note the name collision: in the Deep South, the Caribbean and most of the English-speaking tropics 'pawpaw' means papaya (Carica papaya), an unrelated plant, and 'small-flowered pawpaw' means Asimina parviflora. The custard-fruited understory tree of eastern bottomlands is Asimina triloba and nothing else.",
