    "scientific": "Monarda fistulosa L. (Lamiaceae). Western and Rocky Mountain plants are var. menthifolia, sometimes split off as M. menthifolia - the same plant for this purpose. Two name collisions worth knowing: \"bee balm\" is also, and more properly, the scarlet Monarda didyma of the eastern mountains and gardens, and the \"bergamot\" that flavours Earl Grey is Citrus bergamia, an unrelated citrus.",
